exports[`toHtml > renders the seo-snapshot report 1`] = `
"<article class="dfs-report">
<hgroup id="title"><p class="dfs-kicker">SEO snapshot · October 8, 2026</p><h1>acmeplumbing.example on Google</h1></hgroup>
<p id="answer" class="dfs-lg">acmeplumbing.example gets about 1,241 estimated visits a month from Google, across 312 search terms. 58 of those terms are on page one. 7% of the visits from the top 15 terms come from searches that aren’t about Acme Plumbing’s work, like “riverside coffee” and “best podcasts 2026”.</p>
<dl class="dfs-terms"><div><dt>estimated visits</dt><dd>An estimate of clicks from Google: each term’s searches a month times the share of clicks its position usually gets. It isn’t from analytics.</dd></div><div><dt>page one</dt><dd>Positions #1 to #10, the first page of results. Few people click past it.</dd></div></dl>
<dl class="dfs-stats" id="stats">
<div class="dfs-stat"><dt>Est. visits a month</dt><dd class="dfs-value"><a href="#top-terms-title">1,241</a></dd><dd class="dfs-note">from Google, not analytics</dd></div>
<div class="dfs-stat"><dt>Search terms</dt><dd class="dfs-value"><a href="#positions-title">312</a></dd><dd class="dfs-note">the site shows up for</dd></div>
<div class="dfs-stat"><dt>On page one</dt><dd class="dfs-value"><a href="#positions-title">58</a></dd><dd class="dfs-note">positions #1 to #10, 18 in the top 3</dd></div>
<div class="dfs-stat"><dt>Visits not about your work</dt><dd class="dfs-value"><a href="#off-topic-title">7%</a></dd><dd class="dfs-note">of the top 15 terms’ visits</dd></div>
</dl>
<details id="method">
<summary>How this was measured</summary>
<ul id="method-list">
<li><strong>What:</strong> Every search term acmeplumbing.example shows up for in Google’s top 100, with its position and estimated visits. The tables list the 15 terms that bring the most visits.</li>
<li><strong>Where:</strong> Google in the United States, English. Rankings are national, not what someone searching from one city sees.</li>
<li><strong>When:</strong> Data pulled October 8, 2026.</li>
<li><strong>Source:</strong> DataForSEO Labs, which estimates rankings, searches and visits from its own regular Google crawls.</li>
<li><strong>Sorting:</strong> A term is about your work when it contains a topic word: Plumbing (plumber, plumbing, pipe, repipe, leak, drain, sewer, toilet); Water heaters (water heater); Pumps (sump pump, disposal). Terms with “Acme Plumbing” count as your name. A search for another business or place counts as another name. Everything else is unrelated.</li>
<li><strong>Not measured:</strong> Actual visits, which only Google Search Console or analytics can show, and searches outside Google.</li>
</ul>
</details>
<h2 id="actions-title">What to do</h2>
<p id="actions-intro">Search terms about Acme Plumbing’s work where acmeplumbing.example is on page one or two but outside the top 3, one per page. The top 3 get most of the clicks. Searches for a service or an answer come first, then the most searched.</p>
<div class="dfs-table" id="actions" tabindex="0"><table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Search term</th><th scope="col">Topic</th><th scope="col">Position</th><th scope="col" class="dfs-num">Searches a month</th><th scope="col">Page to improve</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>emergency plumber</td><td>Plumbing</td><td><span class="dfs-badge">#8</span></td><td class="dfs-num">3,600</td><td><code>/</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>water heater repair</td><td>Water heaters</td><td><span class="dfs-badge">#6</span></td><td class="dfs-num">1,900</td><td><code>/water-heaters</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>drain cleaning</td><td>Plumbing</td><td><span class="dfs-badge">#14</span></td><td class="dfs-num">880</td><td><code>/drains</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>tankless water heater install</td><td>Water heaters</td><td><span class="dfs-badge">#11</span></td><td class="dfs-num">480</td><td><code>/water-heaters/tankless</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>garbage disposal repair</td><td>Pumps</td><td><span class="dfs-badge">#5</span></td><td class="dfs-num">320</td><td><code>/disposals</code></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<dl class="dfs-terms"><div><dt>Position</dt><dd>Where the page shows in Google’s results for that search. #1 is the first result; #1 to #10 is page one.</dd></div><div><dt>Searches a month</dt><dd>Average Google searches a month for the term across the United States.</dd></div></dl>
<h2 id="off-topic-title">Searches that aren’t about your work</h2>
<p id="off-topic-note">2 of the top 15 terms bring about 75 estimated visits a month (7%). They’re searches for another business or place, another area or something unrelated. People making them rarely want what acmeplumbing.example offers, so the visit total overstates the traffic that matters. They need no work.</p>
<div class="dfs-table" id="off-topic" tabindex="0"><table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Search term</th><th scope="col">About</th><th scope="col">Position</th><th scope="col" class="dfs-num">Searches a month</th><th scope="col" class="dfs-num">Est. visits</th><th scope="col">Page</th></tr></thead>
