exports[`toMarkdown > renders the ai-visibility report 1`] = `
"# Acme Plumbing in AI answers

_AI visibility · October 8, 2026_

AI answers in DataForSEO’s sample link acmeplumbing.example as a source 3 times and name Acme Plumbing once.

- Citations: **3** (answers linking acmeplumbing.example)
- Mentions: **1** (answers naming Acme Plumbing)
- Topics checked: **2** (acmeplumbing.example a top source in 1)
- Pages cited: **1** (in 1 top question)

## How this was measured

- **What:** How often AI answers name Acme Plumbing (a mention) and link a page on acmeplumbing.example as a source (a citation).
- **Where:** ChatGPT and Google AI Overviews, United States, English.
- **When:** Data pulled October 8, 2026.
- **Source:** DataForSEO LLM Mentions, a large sample of AI answers to real questions. Counts are answers in that sample, not every conversation, and the same question can get a different answer each time.
- **Name matching:** An answer counts as a mention when it contains “Acme Plumbing”. A name made of common words also matches generic phrases, so the mention count can run high.
- **Topics:** For questions containing “water heater repair” and “sewer line repair”, the sites the answers cite most.
- **Questions:** The question with the most AI searches a month whose answers cite acmeplumbing.example.

## What to do

AI tools tend to link pages that answer one question plainly.

- For questions about “water heater repair”, AI answers cite rivalplumbing.example, forum.example and hardware.example most. acmeplumbing.example isn’t in the top 3.

## By platform

A mention is the name in the answer’s text. A citation is a link to the site among its sources. Either can happen without the other.

_mention_: The AI answer names the organization in its text, with or without a link.

_citation_: The AI answer links a page on the site as one of its sources.

| Platform | Mentions | Citations |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| ChatGPT | 1 | 0 |
| Google AI Overviews | 0 | 3 |

## Topics checked

The sites AI answers cite most often for questions containing each topic. “No” means acmeplumbing.example isn’t among those top sites, not that it’s never cited. “Too few answers” means under 10 answers in the sample.

| Topic | acmeplumbing.example a top source | Answers found | Most cited sites |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| water heater repair | No | 90 | rivalplumbing.example, forum.example, hardware.example |
| sewer line repair | Yes | 40 | acmeplumbing.example |

_Answers found_: Answers in the sample to questions that contain the topic.

## Pages AI cites

From the question with the most AI searches a month whose answers link acmeplumbing.example.

| Page | Questions | AI searches a month |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| \`/sewer\` | 1 | 260 |

_AI searches a month_: DataForSEO’s estimate of how often people ask AI tools that question in a month.

## Answers that cite the site

| Question | Where | AI searches a month | Page cited |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| who fixes sewer lines in springfield | Google AI Overviews | 260 | \`/sewer\` |

---

<sub>Data: DataForSEO LLM Mentions, October 8, 2026.</sub>
"
`;

exports[`toMarkdown > renders the backlink-redirects report 1`] = `
"# acmeplumbing.example links that fail today

_Broken link check · October 8, 2026_

3 addresses that other sites link to fail on the live site, https://staging.acmeplumbing.example. Counted per address, they have 62 linking sites.

_linking site_: Other websites with at least one link to that address. Each site counts once.

- Broken: **3** (62 linking sites)
- Redirecting: **3** (land on a live page)
- Unchanged: **1** (same address, still live)
- Behind a login: **1** (couldn’t be checked)

## How this was measured

- **What:** The 100 old acmeplumbing.example addresses with the most linking sites, of 170 that have any. Variants that differ only by http, www, subdomain or tracking tags count as one, which leaves 8 addresses.
- **How:** Each address is requested on https://staging.acmeplumbing.example and followed through any redirects to where it ends up.
- **Results:** Broken: ends on a missing page or an error. Redirecting: forwards to a live page. Unchanged: same address, still live. Behind a login: hit a sign-in page, so it couldn’t be checked.
- **When:** Links counted October 8, 2026; addresses checked October 8, 2026.
- **Source:** DataForSEO Backlinks for the linked addresses and their linking sites. The checks run directly against the site.

## Fix

Each needs a redirect to its closest match, starting with the most linked. Links to a missing page pass no search value, and visitors who follow them land on an error.

| Old address | Type | Result | Linking sites |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: |
| \`/coupons/spring-2019\` | Page | 404 | 46 |
| \`/services/water-heaters/\` | Page | 404 | 11 |
| \`/old-blog/frozen-pipes\` | Page | No response | 5 |

_Result_: 404 means page not found. Any other number is an error the server returned.

> **Sent to the homepage.** 1 inner page redirects to the homepage, which Google treats like a missing page. Point it at its closest match.

## Behind a login

These hit a sign-in page, so they couldn’t be checked.

| Old address | Lands on | Linking sites |
| --- | --- | ---: |
| \`/account\` | \`/login?next=%2Faccount\` | 4 |

## Redirecting

Old addresses that forward to a live page. Check each lands somewhere a visitor would expect.

| Old address | Lands on | Linking sites |
| --- | --- | ---: |
| \`/about-us/\` | \`/about\` | 59 |
| \`/blog/2020/03/hello\` | \`/\` | 3 |
| \`/drains/\` | \`/services/drains\` | 8 |

## Unchanged

| Address | Linking sites |
| --- | ---: |
| \`/\` | 300 |

---

<sub>Data: DataForSEO Backlinks, October 8, 2026.</sub>
"
`;

exports[`toMarkdown > renders the competitor-gap report 1`] = `
"# acmeplumbing.example against competitors on Google

_Competitor gap · October 8, 2026_

rivalplumbing.example and citydrains.example are on Google’s page one for 6 search terms about your work where acmeplumbing.example ranks lower: 2 where it’s further down and 4 where it isn’t in the top 100. Those terms get about 8,790 searches a month.

_page one_: Positions #1 to #10, the first page of results. Few people click past it.

- Behind a competitor: **2** (both rank, the competitor higher)
- Not ranking: **4** (you’re not in the top 100)
- Searches a month: **8,790** (across those terms)
- Competitors: **2** (compared)

## How this was measured

- **What:** Search terms where at least one competitor is on page one (#1 to #10) and acmeplumbing.example is lower or not in the top 100.
- **Competitors:** rivalplumbing.example and citydrains.example.
- **Where:** Google in the United States, English. Rankings are national, not what someone searching from one city sees.
- **When:** Data pulled October 8, 2026.
- **Source:** DataForSEO Labs, which estimates rankings, searches and visits from its own regular Google crawls.
- **Sorting:** A term is about your work when it contains a topic word: Plumbing (plumber, plumbing, pipe, repipe, leak, drain, sewer, toilet); Water heaters (water heater); Pumps (sump pump, disposal). Terms with “Acme Plumbing” count as your name. A search for another business or place counts as another name. Everything else is unrelated.
- **Filter:** For each competitor, up to 100 of its most-searched page-one terms that you also rank for, and up to 100 that you don’t. Terms shared between competitors count once, which leaves 25 terms. 6 are in this report. Left out: 3 terms naming a competitor or another business (like “rival plumbing coupons”), 12 unrelated to your work (like “zip code finder”) and 4 where you already rank ahead.

## What to do

One line per topic, most searched first. Where you rank, improving the page listed is the usual fix. Where you don’t, it’s usually a page that answers the search.

1. **Water heaters:** 2 terms, 5,720 searches a month. The biggest is “tankless water heater”: rivalplumbing.example is #3 and you’re #14 with \`/services\`. Your best position is on “water heater install”: rivalplumbing.example is #4 and you’re #8 with \`/services\`.
2. **Plumbing:** 3 terms, 2,170 searches a month. The biggest is “hydro jetting drain”: citydrains.example is #2 and you’re not in the top 100.
3. **Pumps:** 1 term, 900 searches a month. The biggest is “sump pump installation”: rivalplumbing.example is #7 and you’re not in the top 100.

## By topic

| Topic | Searches a month | Behind | Not ranking | Ahead most often |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| Water heaters | 5,720 | 2 | 0 | \`rivalplumbing.example\` |
| Plumbing | 2,170 | 0 | 3 | \`citydrains.example\` |
| Pumps | 900 | 0 | 1 | \`rivalplumbing.example\` |

_Searches a month_: Average Google searches a month for the term across the United States.

## Behind a competitor

Both sites rank and the competitor is higher. These are usually the quickest to improve, since Google already connects acmeplumbing.example to the search.

| Search term | Topic | Searches a month | Ahead of you | You | Your page |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- | --- |
| tankless water heater | Water heaters | 5,000 | rivalplumbing.example #3 | #14 | \`/services\` |
| water heater install | Water heaters | 720 | rivalplumbing.example #4 | #8 | \`/services\` |

_Ahead of you_: Where the page shows in Google’s results for that search. #1 is the first result; #1 to #10 is page one.

## Not ranking

A competitor is on page one and acmeplumbing.example isn’t in the top 100, usually because no page covers the search.

| Search term | Topic | Searches a month | Who ranks |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| hydro jetting drain | Plumbing | 1,300 | citydrains.example #2, rivalplumbing.example #9 |
| sump pump installation | Pumps | 900 | rivalplumbing.example #7 |
| sewer backflow testing springfield | Plumbing | 480 | citydrains.example #1 |
| slab leak repair | Plumbing | 390 | rivalplumbing.example #6 |

## By competitor

| Competitor | Ahead of you | Only they rank | Only they rank, any term |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| \`rivalplumbing.example\` | 2 | 3 | 140 |
| \`citydrains.example\` | 0 | 2 | 38 |

_Only they rank, any term_: Every term where they’re on page one and acmeplumbing.example isn’t in the top 100, before terms unrelated to your work are left out.

---

<sub>Data: DataForSEO Labs, October 8, 2026.</sub>
"
`;

