exports[`toMarkdown > renders the seo-snapshot report 1`] = `
"# acmeplumbing.example on Google

_SEO snapshot · October 8, 2026_

acmeplumbing.example gets about 1,241 estimated visits a month from Google, across 312 search terms. 58 of those terms are on page one. 7% of the visits from the top 15 terms come from searches that aren’t about Acme Plumbing’s work, like “riverside coffee” and “best podcasts 2026”.

_estimated visits_: An estimate of clicks from Google: each term’s searches a month times the share of clicks its position usually gets. It isn’t from analytics.

_page one_: Positions #1 to #10, the first page of results. Few people click past it.

- Est. visits a month: **1,241** (from Google, not analytics)
- Search terms: **312** (the site shows up for)
- On page one: **58** (positions #1 to #10, 18 in the top 3)
- Visits not about your work: **7%** (of the top 15 terms’ visits)

## How this was measured

- **What:** Every search term acmeplumbing.example shows up for in Google’s top 100, with its position and estimated visits. The tables list the 15 terms that bring the most visits.
- **Where:** Google in the United States, English. Rankings are national, not what someone searching from one city sees.
- **When:** Data pulled October 8, 2026.
- **Source:** DataForSEO Labs, which estimates rankings, searches and visits from its own regular Google crawls.
- **Sorting:** A term is about your work when it contains a topic word: Plumbing (plumber, plumbing, pipe, repipe, leak, drain, sewer, toilet); Water heaters (water heater); Pumps (sump pump, disposal). Terms with “Acme Plumbing” count as your name. A search for another business or place counts as another name. Everything else is unrelated.
- **Not measured:** Actual visits, which only Google Search Console or analytics can show, and searches outside Google.

## What to do

Search terms about Acme Plumbing’s work where acmeplumbing.example is on page one or two but outside the top 3, one per page. The top 3 get most of the clicks. Searches for a service or an answer come first, then the most searched.

| Search term | Topic | Position | Searches a month | Page to improve |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| emergency plumber | Plumbing | #8 | 3,600 | \`/\` |
| water heater repair | Water heaters | #6 | 1,900 | \`/water-heaters\` |
| drain cleaning | Plumbing | #14 | 880 | \`/drains\` |
| tankless water heater install | Water heaters | #11 | 480 | \`/water-heaters/tankless\` |
| garbage disposal repair | Pumps | #5 | 320 | \`/disposals\` |

_Position_: Where the page shows in Google’s results for that search. #1 is the first result; #1 to #10 is page one.

_Searches a month_: Average Google searches a month for the term across the United States.

## Searches that aren’t about your work

2 of the top 15 terms bring about 75 estimated visits a month (7%). They’re searches for another business or place, another area or something unrelated. People making them rarely want what acmeplumbing.example offers, so the visit total overstates the traffic that matters. They need no work.

| Search term | About | Position | Searches a month | Est. visits | Page |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| riverside coffee | Another name or place | #4 | 1,300 | 70 | \`/blog/2023/03/riverside-coffee-opens/\` |
| best podcasts 2026 | Unrelated | #18 | 900 | 5 | \`/blog/podcasts\` |

## Rankings by position

11% of the 312 terms are on page three or later, where almost nobody clicks. Most visits come from page one.

